course: dictionary
lesson: 5312
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. The word keel is a good example. «A bird's strong flight muscles are fixed to a keel on its breastbone.» Here a keel is a long ridge of bone, not a part of a boat. The clue is the bird and its breastbone.
explain: The most common meaning is on a boat. The keel is the long piece along the bottom that keeps the boat steady in the water. In the bird sentence, the keel is also a long ridge that holds something firmly in place, just as the boat's keel holds the boat steady.
explain: Keel is also used in everyday phrases. «To keel over» means to fall over suddenly, especially when fainting. «On an even keel» means calm and steady. These phrases do not mean anything about boats, so read the whole sentence to be sure.
fact: A keel is the long piece along the bottom of a boat that keeps it steady in the water.
fact: «Keel over» is an informal phrase meaning to fall over suddenly, especially when fainting.
fact: «On an even keel» means calm and steady.
fact: In «A bird's strong flight muscles are fixed to a keel on its breastbone», the keel is a long ridge of bone on the breastbone.
fact: The same word can have different meanings, so check the clues in the sentence before you decide.
exercise: «The little boat rocked, but its keel kept it steady.» What is a keel? | The front seat where the captain sits | A small oar used for rowing | A sail made of cloth | *The long piece along the bottom of a boat that keeps it steady
exercise: Lily says the ship began to keel over. What does keel over mean? | *To fall over suddenly | To count the crew | To sail very fast | To paint the bottom of a boat
exercise: «She stayed on an even keel all week, calm and steady.» What does on an even keel mean? | *Calm and steady | Very hungry | Lost at sea | Upside down
test: «A bird's strong flight muscles are fixed to a keel on its breastbone.» What does keel most likely mean here? | A hungry bird | *A long ridge of bone that muscles are fixed to | A kind of wing | A feather
test: Which phrase means calm and steady? | Under the weather | Full steam ahead | *On an even keel | Crack the whip
exam: Ben reads: «The yacht leaned over, but its deep keel kept it upright.» What does keel mean here? | A bright light on a ship | A type of sail | To fall asleep | *The long piece along the bottom of a boat that keeps it upright
